-- Termination, not correctness: a recursive rule is never unfolded (it would
-- not stop), so a rule that calls it must still be analysed, with the call as
-- a leaf. A regression here hangs the suite.

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `all hold` xs IS
    CONSIDER xs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN x AND `all hold` rest

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
      b  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `all hold and b` xs b IF
        `all hold` xs
    AND b
